-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ג/5 — ניצול ימי מחלה ופדיון בעקבות מעבר לרפורמת "עוז לתמורה" (24.2.2013)
-- Sick days in the upper division after Oz LeTmura: accumulation (30 days a
-- year, on a position capped by the reform), conversion of days to hours
-- (the job base times 4.33 from תשע"ב, where it was times 4), how hours are
-- deducted and carried between employers, redemption and reimbursement,
-- and the tables of sick hours a year by job base.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT conventions

§ `חוזר תשע"ג/5 ימי מחלה בעוז לתמורה`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, title, dates and the circular's number; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 State the circular's subject: use, carrying and redemption of sick days; the rules follow.
-- akn:preamble/p11 Points to the takanon, section 1.25.3.1, where the sick-day rules are published; that section is encoded on its own.
-- akn:preamble/p12 Background: the Oz LeTmura agreement changes the conditions of employment, the job bases among them; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 "להלן הפירוט"; no rule.

-- The years the circular speaks of; before תשע"ב the reform was not in
-- force and the multiplier was 4 (2ב).
DECLARE `school year` IS ONE OF
    `a year before תשע"ב`
    `תשע"ב`
    `תשע"ג`
    `תשע"ד`

DECLARE `implementation` IS ONE OF
    `not under the reform`
    `partial implementation`
    `full implementation`

DECLARE `sick-day role` IS ONE OF
    `a teacher`
    `a deputy principal`
    `a principal`

-- ¶13: the changes apply to the employee's position in the upper division
-- only.
@ref akn:preamble/p13
GIVEN `upper-division position` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a position held in the upper division
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position the circular changes` `upper-division position` IS
    `upper-division position`

§§ `1. צבירת ימי מחלה`

-- akn:art_1 Heading of section 1; no rule of its own.

-- 1א: 30 sick days a year (agreement of 1.9.1958), unchanged.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
`sick days a year` MEANS 30

-- 1ב: accumulation is counted in days also above 100%, up to 140% for a
-- teacher and 150% for a principal.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b
GIVEN r IS A `sick-day role`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulable position before the reform` r IS
    IF r EQUALS `a principal` THEN 150% ELSE 140%

-- The days a year accrue in days: 30 for the position held, up to the cap
-- (this one before the reform, 1ג's under it).
GIVEN `position held` IS A NUMBER, `cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick days accrued in a year` `position held` `cap` IS
    `sick days a year` TIMES min `position held` `cap`

-- 1ג: under Oz LeTmura the position for which days accumulate is capped.
-- Partial implementation: 130% for a teacher in תשע"ב and 131% in תשע"ג.
-- Three lines give a cap and a cap "באישור מיוחד": the full-implementation
-- teacher "100% (125% באישור מיוחד)" and the תשע"ד partial teacher "114%
-- (128% באישור מיוחד)", which the corpus prints in order since MMS-426;
-- and the principal, "מנהל( 100% -באישור מיוחד עבור מקרים חריגים – )117%",
-- whose brackets the corpus still prints reordered against the Hebrew, so
-- which figure is the cap and which the cap with special approval is not
-- something its text says: that pair is a named input until the corpus is
-- fixed and re-synced.
@desc A cap on the position for which sick days accumulate, and the cap that applies with special approval.
DECLARE `approval caps` HAS
    `cap without approval`       IS A NUMBER
    `cap with special approval`  IS A NUMBER

-- 1ג ¶2: the full-implementation teacher, 100%, 125% with special approval.
`the full-implementation teacher's caps` MEANS `approval caps` (100%) (125%)

-- 1ג ¶6: the partial-implementation teacher in תשע"ד, 114%, 128% with
-- special approval.
`the 2013/14 partial-implementation teacher's caps` MEANS `approval caps` (114%) (128%)

@desc Circular 2012-13/5, section 1ג seventh paragraph: the principal's cap under the reform and the cap with special approval "for exceptional cases". The corpus prints this line scrambled (MMS-426), so the values are supplied from outside until the corpus is fixed and re-synced.
ASSUME `the principal's caps under the reform` IS AN `approval caps`

GIVEN caps IS AN `approval caps`, `special approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cap that applies` caps `special approval` IS
    IF `special approval` THEN caps's `cap with special approval` ELSE caps's `cap without approval`

@ref akn:art_1__para_c akn:art_1__para_c/p2 akn:art_1__para_c/p3 akn:art_1__para_c/p4 akn:art_1__para_c/p5 akn:art_1__para_c/p6 akn:art_1__para_c/p7
GIVEN r IS A `sick-day role`, i IS AN `implementation`, y IS A `school year`, `special approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulable position` r i y `special approval` IS
    IF r EQUALS `a principal` AND NOT i EQUALS `not under the reform`
    THEN `the cap that applies` `the principal's caps under the reform` `special approval`
    ELSE CONSIDER i
         WHEN `not under the reform`  THEN `the accumulable position before the reform` r
         WHEN `full implementation`   THEN `the cap that applies` `the full-implementation teacher's caps` `special approval`
         WHEN `partial implementation` THEN
             CONSIDER y
             WHEN `תשע"ב` THEN 130%
             WHEN `תשע"ג` THEN 131%
             WHEN `תשע"ד` THEN `the cap that applies` `the 2013/14 partial-implementation teacher's caps` `special approval`
             WHEN `a year before תשע"ב` THEN `the accumulable position before the reform` r

#ASSERT `the accumulable position` `a teacher` `full implementation` `תשע"ד` FALSE EQUALS 100%
#ASSERT `the accumulable position` `a teacher` `full implementation` `תשע"ד` TRUE EQUALS 125%
#ASSERT `the accumulable position` `a teacher` `partial implementation` `תשע"ד` FALSE EQUALS 114%
#ASSERT `the accumulable position` `a teacher` `partial implementation` `תשע"ד` TRUE EQUALS 128%

-- 1ג ¶8-¶13: a teacher entitled to a mother's position adds to these caps:
-- in partial implementation 8.6% (תשע"ב), 8.3% (תשע"ג), 7.6% (תשע"ד); in
-- full implementation 7%.
@ref akn:art_1__para_c/p8 akn:art_1__para_c/p9 akn:art_1__para_c/p10 akn:art_1__para_c/p11 akn:art_1__para_c/p12 akn:art_1__para_c/p13
GIVEN i IS AN `implementation`, y IS A `school year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the mother's addition` i y IS
    CONSIDER i
    WHEN `full implementation` THEN 7%
    WHEN `partial implementation` THEN
        CONSIDER y
        WHEN `תשע"ב` THEN 8.6%
        WHEN `תשע"ג` THEN 8.3%
        WHEN `תשע"ד` THEN 7.6%
        OTHERWISE 0
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN r IS A `sick-day role`, i IS AN `implementation`, y IS A `school year`, `special approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `entitled to a mother's position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulable position with the mother's addition` r i y `special approval` `entitled to a mother's position` IS
    `the accumulable position` r i y `special approval`
    PLUS (IF `entitled to a mother's position` THEN `the mother's addition` i y ELSE 0)

-- 1ד: no ceiling on the sick days one may accumulate.
@ref akn:art_1__para_d
GIVEN `days accumulated` IS A NUMBER, `days accrued this year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the accumulated balance` `days accumulated` `days accrued this year` IS
    `days accumulated` PLUS `days accrued this year`

-- 1ה: days not used with other teaching employers accumulate too; carrying
-- them is by the collective agreements.
@ref akn:art_1__para_e
GIVEN `days from other teaching employers` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days carried from other employers` `days from other teaching employers` IS
    sum `days from other teaching employers`

§§ `2. ניצול ימי מחלה בפועל וגרירתם`

-- akn:art_2 Heading of section 2; no rule of its own.

-- 2א: the takanon converts days to "sick-day hours" by the job base times
-- 4, subject to the position; ¶2 says the takanon gives examples. 2ב: from
-- תשע"ב the base is multiplied by 4.33, for every upper-division teacher,
-- joined to the reform or not (section 15(ב) of the agreement).
@ref akn:art_2__para_a akn:art_2__para_a/p2 akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_b/p2
`the takanon's multiplier` MEANS 4

GIVEN y IS A `school year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours multiplier in the upper division` y IS
    IF y EQUALS `a year before תשע"ב` THEN `the takanon's multiplier` ELSE 4.33

GIVEN `job base` IS A NUMBER, `position` IS A NUMBER, y IS A `school year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick-day hours a year` `job base` `position` y IS
    `job base` TIMES `the hours multiplier in the upper division` y TIMES `position`

-- 2ב ¶3: what was computed up to תשע"ב by the multiplier 4 is not changed
-- and is carried to later years as days.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b/p3
GIVEN `hours computed by 4` IS A NUMBER, `job base then` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days carried from before תשע"ב` `hours computed by 4` `job base then` IS
    (`hours computed by 4` DIVIDED BY (`job base then` TIMES `the takanon's multiplier`)) TIMES `sick days a year`

-- 2ג-2ד: in full implementation a full position is 40 weekly hours; the
-- hours quota grows with the base (the tables below), the days do not, and
-- an absence deducts the larger number of hours the employee works on the
-- day.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c akn:art_2__para_d
`a full position's weekly hours in full implementation` MEANS 40

-- 2ה: a justified absence (medical documents) deducts the hours of the
-- employee's timetable for the day or days — support and individual hours
-- missed included.
@ref akn:art_2__para_e
GIVEN `frontal hours that day` IS A NUMBER, `individual hours that day` IS A NUMBER, `support hours that day` IS A NUMBER, `justified by medical documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick hours deducted for the day` `frontal hours that day` `individual hours that day` `support hours that day` `justified by medical documents` IS
    IF `justified by medical documents`
    THEN `frontal hours that day` PLUS `individual hours that day` PLUS `support hours that day`
    ELSE 0

-- 2ו: when the days with the present employer run out, the employee may
-- carry days between employers by the agreements; they come over as days
-- and are converted to hours for use.
@ref akn:art_2__para_f akn:art_2__para_f/p2
GIVEN `hours left with this employer` IS A NUMBER, `days with earlier employers` IS A NUMBER, `job base` IS A NUMBER, y IS A `school year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours available after carrying` `hours left with this employer` `days with earlier employers` `job base` y IS
    IF `hours left with this employer` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `hours left with this employer`
    ELSE (`days with earlier employers` DIVIDED BY `sick days a year`) TIMES `sick-day hours a year` `job base` 1 y

§§ `3. פדיון ימי מחלה בלתי מנוצלים`

-- akn:art_3 Heading of section 3; no rule of its own.

-- 3א: redemption follows the rules in force before the agreement; an
-- employee entitled to it from the owner under them is entitled to it now.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a
GIVEN `entitled under the rules before the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to redeem unused sick days` `entitled under the rules before the agreement` IF
    `entitled under the rules before the agreement`

-- 3ב: the owner submits a request for reimbursement as before; the
-- Ministry examines it under the reimbursement procedure and transfers the
-- payment. No deadline is set: the time is the redemption's.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b
DECLARE `sick-day action` IS ONE OF
    `submit a reimbursement request`
    `examine the request under the reimbursement procedure`
    `convert the hours to days`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sick-day action`
DECIDE `reimbursement of redeemed days` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MAY   `submit a reimbursement request`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
           MUST  `examine the request under the reimbursement procedure`)

-- akn:art_3__para_b/p2 The heading "הערות כלליות"; no rule.

-- 3ב.1: the owner keeps the count in hours for each employee and at the end
-- of each year converts it to days (keeping the base it was computed on),
-- for the case of a move to another owner. School months: August = 12.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sick-day action`
DECIDE `the yearly conversion to days` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `convert the hours to days`
    WITHIN `month number` August
    LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשע\"ג/5, 3ב.1: at the end of each year the hours are converted to days"

GIVEN `hours left` IS A NUMBER, `job base` IS A NUMBER, y IS A `school year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours as days` `hours left` `job base` y IS
    (`hours left` DIVIDED BY `sick-day hours a year` `job base` 1 y) TIMES `sick days a year`

-- 3ב.2: hours up to 100% of a position and hours above it are counted
-- separately, because their use and redemption values differ.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2
GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER, `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours up to a full position` `hours` `position` IS
    IF `position` AT MOST 1 THEN `hours` ELSE `hours` DIVIDED BY `position`

GIVEN `hours` IS A NUMBER, `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours above a full position` `hours` `position` IS
    `hours` MINUS `hours up to a full position` `hours` `position`

-- akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p2 The contact line for questions; no rule.
-- akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p3 The tables' common title ("שעות ימי מחלה לפי בסיס משרה שונים"); no rule.

§§ `טבלאות שעות מחלה`

-- The three tables as printed: each row a job base and the sick hours a
-- year for a full position. The PDF heads the first "טבלת מורים" and the
-- third "טבלת סגן מנהל", but the first's rows are deputies and the third's
-- teachers; the rows say what they are, and this file follows the rows.
DECLARE `sick-hours row` HAS
    `row role`           IS A `sick-day role`
    `row implementation` IS AN `implementation`
    `row base`           IS A NUMBER
    `row hours`          IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/t1 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/t2
`the first table (deputy rows)` MEANS
    LIST `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `not under the reform`    24 96,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 26 112.58,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 28 121.24,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 28 121.24,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 28 121.24,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 29 125.57,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 30 129.9,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 30 129.9,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 30 129.9,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 31 134.23,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 32 138.56,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 32 138.56,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 34 147.22,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 34 147.22,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 35 151.55,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `partial implementation` 36 155.88,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `full implementation`    36 155.88,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `full implementation`    38 164.54,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `full implementation`    38 164.54,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `full implementation`    39 168.87,
         `sick-hours row` `a deputy principal` `full implementation`    40 173.2

@ref akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/t1 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/t3 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/t2
`the principal table` MEANS
    LIST `sick-hours row` `a principal` `not under the reform`    24 96,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 35 151.55,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 36 155.88,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 36 155.88,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 37 160.21,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 37 160.21,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 37 160.21,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 38 164.54,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 38 164.54,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `full implementation`    38 164.54,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `partial implementation` 39 168.87,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `full implementation`    39 168.87,
         `sick-hours row` `a principal` `full implementation`    40 173.2

@ref akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p7 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/t1 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/t4
`the third table (teacher rows)` MEANS
    LIST `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `not under the reform`    24 96,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 26 112.58,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 28 121.24,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 28 121.24,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 30 129.9,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 30 129.9,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 32 138.56,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 32 138.56,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 34 147.22,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `partial implementation` 36 155.88,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `full implementation`    36 155.88,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `full implementation`    38 164.54,
         `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `full implementation`    40 173.2

`all the table rows` MEANS
    concat (LIST `the first table (deputy rows)`, `the principal table`, `the third table (teacher rows)`)

-- Every reform row of the tables is its base times 4.33, as 2ב says.
`every reform row is its base times 4.33` MEANS
    all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row implementation` EQUALS `not under the reform`
                       OR r's `row hours` EQUALS r's `row base` TIMES 4.33)
        `all the table rows`
#ASSERT `every reform row is its base times 4.33`

-- The age-hours notes. The principal's note (¶87): full age hours go with
-- teaching 2/3 of the 24-hour base in class; a principal teaches less and so
-- has half. Notes 1-2 (¶116-¶118): a deputy teaching less than 2/3 of the
-- base of 24 has half, 2/3 and more the full entitlement. The full
-- entitlement is what the rows print: 4 hours above 55, 2 above 50.
-- Convention thresholds.above (conventions.toml): the rows print "מעל גיל 50"
-- and "מעל גיל 55", so neither 50 nor 55 itself is above: 50 has none and
-- 55 has the 2 hours.
@ref akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p6 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p8 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p9 akn:art_3__para_b__subpara_2/p10
GIVEN r IS A `sick-day role`, `frontal hours in class` IS A NUMBER, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `age hours off the base` r `frontal hours in class` `age` IS
    IF NOT `age` `is above` 50
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF r EQUALS `a principal` OR (r EQUALS `a deputy principal` AND `frontal hours in class` LESS THAN (2 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES 24)
         THEN (IF `age` `is above` 55 THEN 4 ELSE 2) DIVIDED BY 2
         ELSE IF `age` `is above` 55 THEN 4 ELSE 2

-- The deputy rows agree with the notes: partial implementation תשע"ג base
-- 32, above 55 with the full entitlement, is base 28 (121.24 hours).
#ASSERT 32 MINUS `age hours off the base` `a deputy principal` 20 57 EQUALS 28
#ASSERT 37 MINUS `age hours off the base` `a principal` 5 57 EQUALS 35

-- F-2012-13_tashag_05-a: each table's first row prices "עולם ישן" — not
-- under the reform — in "חט"ב וחט"ע" at base 24 times 4: 96 hours. 2ב says
-- that from תשע"ב every upper-division teacher's base is multiplied by
-- 4.33, "even if they have not yet joined the reform": 103.92 hours.
`the old-world row` MEANS
    `sick-hours row` `a teacher` `not under the reform` 24 96

`2ב and the tables give an upper-division teacher outside the reform different hours` MEANS
    NOT (`the old-world row`'s `row hours` EQUALS `sick-day hours a year` 24 1 `תשע"ג`)
#ASSERT `2ב and the tables give an upper-division teacher outside the reform different hours`

-- akn:conclusions The greeting and the signature; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

#ASSERT `sick-day hours a year` 40 1 `תשע"ג` EQUALS 173.2
#ASSERT `sick-day hours a year` 36 0.5 `תשע"ד` EQUALS 77.94
#ASSERT `the accumulable position with the mother's addition` `a teacher` `partial implementation` `תשע"ג` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 139.3%
#ASSERT `sick days accrued in a year` 1.4 (`the accumulable position` `a teacher` `partial implementation` `תשע"ג` FALSE) EQUALS 39.3
#ASSERT `sick hours deducted for the day` 4 1 2 TRUE EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `hours as days` 86.6 40 `תשע"ג` EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `days carried from before תשע"ב` 48 24 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT NOT (`age hours off the base` `a deputy principal` 10 57 EQUALS 4)
#ASSERT `age hours off the base` `a teacher` 20 50 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `age hours off the base` `a teacher` 20 51 EQUALS 2

#TRACE `the yearly conversion to days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `convert the hours to days` AT 12
#TRACE `reimbursement of redeemed days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `submit a reimbursement request` AT 3
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `examine the request under the reimbursement procedure` AT 4

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular over a finite space: every role, implementation and year
-- whose cap the text states, job bases 24 to 40, positions in tenths from 0
-- to 1.5, ages 40 to 65, frontal hours 0 to 24.

`every role` MEANS LIST `a teacher`, `a deputy principal`, `a principal`
`every year` MEANS LIST `a year before תשע"ב`, `תשע"ב`, `תשע"ג`, `תשע"ד`
`tenths to 1.5` MEANS map (GIVEN k YIELD k DIVIDED BY 10) (range 0 15)

-- 2א-2ב over every year, base and position: the hours are the base times 4
-- before תשע"ב and times 4.33 from it, times the position; they never fall
-- with a larger base or position; and 3ב.1's conversion back to days gives
-- 30 days a year for the position, whatever the base.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN y YIELD
                all (GIVEN b YIELD
                        all (GIVEN p YIELD
                                LET h MEANS `sick-day hours a year` b p y
                                IN      h EQUALS b TIMES (IF y EQUALS `a year before תשע"ב` THEN 4 ELSE 4.33) TIMES p
                                    AND h AT MOST `sick-day hours a year` (b PLUS 1) p y
                                    AND h AT MOST `sick-day hours a year` b (p PLUS 0.1) y
                                    AND `hours as days` h b y EQUALS 30 TIMES p)
                            `tenths to 1.5`)
                    (range 24 40))
            `every year`

-- 1ב-1ג where the text states the cap (outside the reform, and partial
-- implementation in תשע"ב and תשע"ג): a principal's cap outside the reform
-- is above a teacher's; partial implementation's rises from תשע"ב to תשע"ג;
-- the days accrued never pass 30 times the cap and never fall with a larger
-- position; 1ג's mother's addition in partial implementation falls from year
-- to year and is nothing outside the reform.
`a principal's cap outside the reform is above a teacher's` MEANS
    `the accumulable position` `a teacher` `not under the reform` `תשע"ג` FALSE
    LESS THAN `the accumulable position` `a principal` `not under the reform` `תשע"ג` FALSE
#ASSERT `a principal's cap outside the reform is above a teacher's`
`the partial-implementation cap rises from תשע"ב to תשע"ג` MEANS
    `the accumulable position` `a teacher` `partial implementation` `תשע"ב` FALSE
    LESS THAN `the accumulable position` `a teacher` `partial implementation` `תשע"ג` FALSE
#ASSERT `the partial-implementation cap rises from תשע"ב to תשע"ג`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD
                all (GIVEN p YIELD
                        LET cap MEANS `the accumulable position` r `not under the reform` `תשע"ג` FALSE
                            d MEANS `sick days accrued in a year` p cap
                        IN      d AT MOST 30 TIMES cap
                            AND d AT MOST `sick days accrued in a year` (p PLUS 0.1) cap)
                    `tenths to 1.5`)
            `every role`
`the mother's addition falls from year to year and is nothing outside the reform` MEANS
        `the mother's addition` `partial implementation` `תשע"ד` LESS THAN `the mother's addition` `partial implementation` `תשע"ג`
    AND `the mother's addition` `partial implementation` `תשע"ג` LESS THAN `the mother's addition` `partial implementation` `תשע"ב`
    AND all (GIVEN y YIELD `the mother's addition` `not under the reform` y EQUALS 0) `every year`
#ASSERT `the mother's addition falls from year to year and is nothing outside the reform`

-- 2ה and 3ב.2 over hours and positions: a justified day deducts its hours
-- and an unjustified one none; the hours up to and above a full position
-- add up to the whole, and above a full position there are none at 100% or
-- less.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN f YIELD
                all (GIVEN j YIELD
                        `sick hours deducted for the day` f 1 2 j EQUALS (IF j THEN f PLUS 3 ELSE 0))
                    (LIST TRUE, FALSE))
            (range 0 8)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN p YIELD
                    `hours up to a full position` 120 p PLUS `hours above a full position` 120 p EQUALS 120
                AND (`hours above a full position` 120 p EQUALS 0) EQUALS (p AT MOST 1))
            (LIST 0.5, 1, 1.2, 1.4)

-- The tables: each row is its role's, and within each table the hours
-- never fall as the base grows.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN pair YIELD
                LET rows MEANS at pair 0
                IN  all (GIVEN i YIELD (at rows i)'s `row hours` AT MOST (at rows (i PLUS 1))'s `row hours`)
                        (range 0 (count rows MINUS 2)))
            (LIST (LIST `the first table (deputy rows)`), (LIST `the principal table`), (LIST `the third table (teacher rows)`))

-- The age notes over every role, age and frontal load: the age hours are
-- none up to 50 and never more than the full entitlement (4 above 55, 2
-- above 50); a principal has half of it, a teacher all of it, and a deputy
-- all of it exactly from two thirds of 24 frontal hours.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD
                all (GIVEN a YIELD
                        all (GIVEN f YIELD
                                LET h MEANS `age hours off the base` r f a
                                    full MEANS IF a AT MOST 50 THEN 0 ELSE IF a GREATER THAN 55 THEN 4 ELSE 2
                                IN      h AT MOST full
                                    AND h EQUALS (IF r EQUALS `a principal` OR (r EQUALS `a deputy principal` AND f LESS THAN 16)
                                                  THEN full DIVIDED BY 2 ELSE full))
                            (range 0 24))
                    (range 40 65))
            `every role`
